    "worker_judgment_notes": "Selected the official IMPD Transparency Portal FeatureServer layer IMPD_Public_Data/Incidents_Public because it is the first official runnable point feed found with 2024 records, stable row identity via GlobalID/OBJECTID, epoch-ms OccurredFrom dates, NIBRSClassCode offense categories, and WGS84 Latitude/Longitude point coordinates. Older Open Indy UCR annual tables are official Part 1 feeds but were published only through 2021 plus an empty current-year table, so they do not satisfy the 2024 point-feed requirement. This contract is share-lane only: raw feed rows are public incident/offense rows and must not be promoted as annual totals. Rape is intentionally omitted because the public point layer inspected did not expose N11 sex-offense rows, while the separate NIBRS_Inc_DBonly table showed N11A/N11B/N11C/N11D categories but no point geometry. The jurisdiction_id and state_fips come from state/controls/jurisdiction_controls_2024.parquet for Indianapolis city (balance); bounds are broad municipal block-group bounds computed from the local TIGER block-group file joined through state/geometry/block_group_to_jurisdiction_crosswalk.parquet, so the runner can spatially join incidents to municipal block groups.",
